[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5297275667","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122369#issuecomment-5297275667","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122369","id":5297275667,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABO74DEw","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-14T19:22:22Z","updated_at":"2026-08-14T19:22:22Z","body":"> selecting something is better than selecting nothing.\n\nThat's questionable. Selected node not only affects the inspector, but also editor viewport. Like, if you open a scene and the editor selects tilemap, you can't select nodes in the 2D editor, you have to deselect the node first.\n\nThe editor currently remembers selected nodes in each scenes, so if you open a scene and nothing is selected, it just means that you didn't have anything selected when the scene was closed. I think it's a sensible behavior.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5297275667/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5297515936","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122369#issuecomment-5297515936","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122369","id":5297515936,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABO8GtoA","user":{"login":"Arecher","id":10502115,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTAyMTE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10502115?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher","html_url":"https://github.com/Arecher","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-14T19:50:22Z","updated_at":"2026-08-14T19:57:49Z","body":"> That's questionable. Selected node not only affects the inspector, but also editor viewport. Like, if you open a scene and the editor selects tilemap, you can't select nodes in the 2D editor, you have to deselect the node first.\n\nThat's a valid concern, but if the root node of the scene is a TileMap, this is likely a TileMap specific scene, so working on the TileMap is one of the more common usecases and therefore unlikely to be disruptive all the time.\n\n> The editor currently remembers selected nodes in each scenes, so if you open a scene and nothing is selected, it just means that you didn't have anything selected when the scene was closed. \n\nThat behaviour is definitely bugged in that case. Selecting a node, closing the scene and reopening the scene does not preserve the node selection. *(From reading the PRs, probably only for opening from an empty tab)*\n\n<img width=\"511\" height=\"300\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/71161975-b26b-40a1-ad63-8edb5d4cda2a\" />\n\nEven if you save beforehand, this issue still exists.\n\nBut if the behaviour for reselecting the last-selected node is fixed, that should be preferred over selecting the top-most node. However, if no last-selected node exists, I still think selecting the top-most node in the SceneTree is a better outcome than selecting none. While it might be disruptive in niche circumstances, all it would need is a single selection in the SceneTree, which is exactly the same amount of work it would currently take.\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5297515936/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5297541418","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122369#issuecomment-5297541418","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122369","id":5297541418,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABO8IRKg","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-14T19:53:31Z","updated_at":"2026-08-14T19:53:31Z","body":"Yeah that bug has to be fixed.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5297541418/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5301430842","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122369#issuecomment-5301430842","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122369","id":5301430842,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABO_1qOg","user":{"login":"Linie3","id":75386862,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1Mzg2ODYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75386862?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Linie3","html_url":"https://github.com/Linie3","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Linie3/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Linie3/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Linie3/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Linie3/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Linie3/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Linie3/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Linie3/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Linie3/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Linie3/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-15T08:43:32Z","updated_at":"2026-08-15T08:43:32Z","body":"So @distmed's #122420 successfully fixes the bug, but I don't think it should close this issues. If the behaviour of selecting the root node upon opening a Scene without prior selection is desirable, my PR #122392 would implement this. I have already tested that both PRs also work together correctly.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5301430842/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]